     ↓
Deploy service
     ↓
Monitor service
```

Everything happens inside one portal.

---

# 3️⃣ Service Catalog (Key Component)

Spotify’s IDP revolves around a **service catalog**.

Each service has metadata like:

```text
Service Name
Owner Team
Repository
Runtime
Dependencies
Alerts
On-call team
```

Example entry:

```text
Service: payments-service
Owner: Payments Team
Repo: github.com/company/payments
Language: Go
Dependencies: users-service, postgres
```

This helps engineers quickly understand **who owns what and how systems connect**.

---

# 4️⃣ Plugin Architecture

Backstage uses a **plugin system**, allowing teams to integrate any tool.

Common plugins include:

* CI/CD pipelines
* Kubernetes
* monitoring dashboards
* documentation
* incident management

Example plugin list:

```text
CI/CD plugin
Kubernetes plugin
Grafana plugin
PagerDuty plugin
GitHub plugin
```

This makes the platform **extensible and customizable**.

---

# 5️⃣ Self-Service Developer Workflows

Spotify’s IDP provides **self-service infrastructure and service creation**.

Example:

```text
Create Service
   ↓
Select template
   ↓
Repo + pipeline + infra created automatically
